WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:06.400
In 1875, John Henry Newman, a
Catholic, imagined proposing a toast.

2
00:00:06.450 --> 00:00:11.410
His toast: to conscience first,
and to the Pope afterwards.

3
00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:16.150
Jesus warned that it is easier for a camel
to go through a needle's eye than for

4
00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:18.880
a rich man to enter into God's Kingdom.

5
00:00:18.930 --> 00:00:23.440
And in the past, some Christian states
persecuted people for their beliefs.

6
00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:26.940
So should a Christian follow
conscience over the Church,

7
00:00:26.990 --> 00:00:30.440
give wealth away, and
tolerate every belief?

8
00:00:30.490 --> 00:00:34.830
In this mission, you'll weigh Christian
teaching on wealth and tolerance against

9
00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:37.850
Bentham, Marx, Locke and Mill.

10
00:00:37.900 --> 00:00:42.900
Then you'll open up conscience itself,
and meet the thinkers who doubt it.

11
00:00:42.950 --> 00:00:46.570
Your mission: weigh up when a
Christian should follow conscience,

12
00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:49.160
share wealth and tolerate other beliefs.
